  "schedule": "3 non-consecutive days (Mon/Wed/Fri). Workouts A, B, C, D rotate continuously: week 1 A-B-C, week 2 D-A-B, week 3 C-D-A, and so on for 12 weeks.",
  "progression": {
    "type": "DOUBLE_PROGRESSION",
    "description": "Program text: within each rep range, keep the same weight and aim for more reps each week until you have mastered it; e.g. in a 5-8 range, stay at the weight until you can do 9 reps, then go heavier but still able to do at least 5, and stay there until you can do at least 9 again. In-app week 2 note: start with last week's weights, aim for 1 more rep than before until you hit the top of the target range, then increase weight by 5-10 lb and work within the range. Each set of the pyramid progresses on its own rep range. The source gives one 5-10 lb increment for all lifts; the upper 2.5 kg / lower 5 kg split in incrementKg is a metric rounding choice for this app, not the author's.",
    "incrementKg": {
      "upper": 2.5,
      "lower": 5
    },
    "deload": "No deload or stall rule is stated by the author."
